<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stormarn</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stormarn is a historical region and present-day district in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was one of the three <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> districts north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, alongside Holstein and Dithmarschen, with Hamburg as its chief centre. In 1111 it was granted, with Holstein, to Adolf I of Schauenburg, and it remained part of Holstein thereafter.</p></div>
